<title>PAKISTAN: Pakistan reserves slide to $1.262 bln in October.</title>
<headline>Pakistan reserves slide to $1.262 bln in October.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1996-11-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pakistan's foreign exchange reserves fell to $1.262 billion in October from $1.865 billion in September, compared to $1.963 billion in October 1995, the State (central) Bank of Pakistan said on Tuesday.  </p>
<p>A foreign banker said debt repayments scheduled in October and higher imports might have drained the reserves, which included $543 million within Pakistan and $30 million outside.</p>
<p>Following is Pakistan's monthly foreign reserves position:</p>
<p>    (MLN DLRS)		OCT	  SEPT	 OCT 95</p>
<p>TOTAL			   1,262	1,865	1,963</p>
<p>Forex in Pakistan	     543	  569	1,016</p>
<p>Forex outside Pakistan	 30	  560	  228</p>
<p>Gold coins and bullion	676	  734	  706</p>
<p>Special Drawing Rights	 13	    2	   13</p>
<p>-- Karachi newsroom 9221-5685192</p>
</text>
